    "result_text": "Done. The full build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe rule computes a derived `membershipTier` field returned on the owner response. Two changes implement it:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression that computes the tier when mapping `Owner \u2192 OwnerDto`:\n   - `SILVER` when `namesakeCount == 0` **and** an email is present (non-null, non-blank)\n   - `BRONZE` otherwise\n\nThe logic lives alongside the existing derived fields (`membershipNumber`, `displayName`, `initials`) rather than in a new OfficeFloor step, since those response-shaping computations are all done in the mapper. `namesakeCount` is set upstream by the existing `AssignNamesakeCount` step in `owners.POST.yml`, and email presence uses the already-normalized value.\n\nTests: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 both `coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail` and `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail` pass, and the full suite builds green.",
